      "name": "createEnvelope",
      "description": "Creates a new Docusign envelope from an EXISTING Docusign template or from documents provided via a remote URL.\n\nFor template-based envelopes:\n  Use createEnvelopeFromTemplate (the primary tool for template-based envelopes). If using createEnvelope directly, provide envelopeDefinition.templateId (call getTemplates first to find the correct ID).\n\nFor URL-based document envelopes:\n  Provide envelopeDefinition.documents with remoteUrl.\n  Each document requires: documentId, name, and remoteUrl (publicly accessible HTTPS URL, max 25 MB per file).\n  At least one signer in recipients is required.\n\nCRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:\n(1) NEVER call with a templateId unless the user has explicitly identified a specific template.\n(2) NEVER auto-select, guess, or substitute a \"similar\" template.\n(3) DO NOT generate documentBase64 content \u2014 this tool does not accept base64 file uploads.\n(4) Recipients and tabs are optional when using templateId (the template may already define them).\n(5) When using remoteUrl documents, recipients with at least one signer are required.\n\nGOTCHA \u2014 Adding documents to an existing envelope is not supported:\nThe updateEnvelope tool does not support adding documents. If a draft envelope needs a document,\ncreate a new envelope with the document included from the start.",
